<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>SELF-DESTRUCT OVEN - Screenplay</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: 8.5in 11in; margin: 1in 1in 1in 1.5in; }
        @media print { body { margin: 0; padding: 0; } .no-print { display: none; } }
        body { font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 6in; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1in 0; background-color: #f5f5f5; }
        .screenplay { background-color: white; padding: 1in 1.5in; box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); }
        .title-page { text-align: center; padding-top: 3in; page-break-after: always; }
        .title { font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.5in; }
        .credit { font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0.25in; }
        .author { font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 2in; }
        .contact { font-size: 10pt; text-align: left; margin-top: 2in; }
        .scene-heading { font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 2em; margin-bottom: 1em; }
        .action { margin-bottom: 1em; }
        .character { margin-left: 2.2in; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 0; text-transform: uppercase; }
        .parenthetical { margin-left: 1.7in; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; }
        .dialogue { margin-left: 1.2in; margin-right: 1.5in; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-top: 0; }
        .transition { text-align: right; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
        .centered { text-align: center; margin: 1em 0; font-weight: bold; }
        .act-heading { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 2em 0 1em 0; text-decoration: underline; }
        .print-button { position: fixed; top: 20px; right: 20px; padding: 10px 20px; background-color: #007bff; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.2); }
        .print-button:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <button class="print-button no-print" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save as PDF</button>
    <div class="screenplay">
        <div class="title-page">
            <div class="title">SELF-DESTRUCT OVEN</div>
            <div class="credit">An SNL Sketch</div>
            <div class="author">by<br>Screenplays Project</div>
            <div class="contact">Draft date: 2026-02-07<br>Runtime: 4:00 minutes<br>Format: Single-camera or live sketch<br>Setting: Corporate boardroom</div>
        </div>
        <div class="act-heading">ACT 1: SETUP</div>
        <div class="transition">FADE IN:</div>
        <div class="scene-heading">EXT. FLAMETEK INDUSTRIES - DAY</div>
        <div class="centered">TITLE CARD: "FLAMETEK INDUSTRIES - EXECUTIVE BOARDROOM"</div>
        <div class="scene-heading">INT. FLAMETEK INDUSTRIES - EXECUTIVE BOARDROOM - DAY</div>
        <div class="action">A sleek corporate boardroom. Long conference table with six chairs. A presentation screen behind the head of the table. Coffee service on a side table. Everyone is in business attire.</div>
        <div class="character">**CHARACTERS PRESENT**:</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- RONALD "RON" PEMBERTON III (CEO, 60s, New England accent) - seated at head of table, half-asleep with coffee</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- BRENDA HARTFORD (CMO, 50s, Mid-Atlantic corporate speak) - standing by presentation screen</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- DEREK CHEN (VP Product Safety, 30s, nervous energy) - seated with stack of folders</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- MAURICE LEBLANC (Head of Legal, 50s, French accent) - seated calmly</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- TODD BRINKMAN (VP Engineering, 40s, Midwestern monotone) - already sweating</div>
        <div class="dialogue">- JESSICA RAMIREZ (Junior Associate, 20s, Valley Girl uptalk) - seated with tablet and excessive enthusiasm</div>
        <div class="action">BRENDA stands at the presentation screen, clicker in hand, beaming with corporate enthusiasm. RON's head is tilted back, eyes closed. DEREK nervously shuffles papers. TODD wipes his forehead with a handkerchief. MAURICE examines his nails. JESSICA types eagerly on her tablet.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(overly enthusiastic)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Good morning, everyone! Thank you SO much for making time for this incredibly important strategic alignment session!</div>
        <div class="action">Ron's head snaps up suddenly.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(confused, groggy)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Is this the refrigerator meeting?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(still smiling)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">No sir, this is the oven meeting.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(genuinely confused)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We make ovens?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes sir, for thirty-five years.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nodding slowly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Huh. I thought we made refrigerators.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quietly, wiping forehead)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We... we don't make refrigerators, sir.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(disappointed)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh.</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(beat)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We should look into that.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(typing enthusiastically)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Literally writing that down!</div>
        <div class="action">Derek raises his hand tentatively.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Um, if we could get started? This is actually pretty urgent—</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(cutting him off, still beaming)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Absolutely, Derek! Love the energy! So, as you all know, our FlameClean 3000 self-cleaning oven has been on the market for six months now, and we've received some very... passionate customer feedback!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calmly, French accent)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly passionate.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing up, urgent)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Brenda, we need to talk about the safety data. I've been tracking incidents and—</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(interrupting, gesturing grandly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">And we are SO grateful for your diligence, Derek! Why don't you share those numbers with the team?</div>
        <div class="action">Derek clicks his remote. A slide appears showing a graph with alarming upward trend.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nervously)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Okay, so... in the past six months, we've had 847 reported incidents of the self-cleaning function causing... um...</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(swallows hard)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">...house fires.</div>
        <div class="action">Pause. JESSICA drops her stylus. TODD wipes his forehead more vigorously. MAURICE doesn't react. RON squints at the screen.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(confused)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Is that a lot?</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(incredulous)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! That's— yes, sir, that's a lot! That represents approximately 40% of all units sold!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(gasping)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh my god.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(gaining confidence)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Exactly! Which is why I'm recommending we issue an immediate product recall and—</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(jumping in, still positive)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Okay, okay, let's pump the brakes on the R-word, Derek!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(correcting)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Alleged fires, Derek. Alleged.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(frustrated)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">No, Maurice, actual fires. Confirmed fires. Documented fires with photo evidence and fire department reports!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(unruffled)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly confirmed.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(exasperated)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">They're not allegedly— there are literally houses that are no longer standing!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(thoughtfully)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly no longer standing.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Maurice, impressed)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's literally so smart.</div>
        <div class="action">Ron raises his hand like a confused student.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Question. What's the difference between a bug and a feature?</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(technical, nervous)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Well, technically, sir, a bug is an unintended flaw in the design, whereas a feature is an intentional—</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(interrupting, excited, moving to center stage)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">EXACTLY! Thank you, Todd! And that's exactly what we need to discuss today!</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(turning to face everyone)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Is this really a problem... or is this an opportunity?</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing, emphatic)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">It's definitely a problem!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pointing at Derek, then sweeping her arm dramatically)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Or... and hear me out... what if this isn't a bug...</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(dramatic pause)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What if this is a FEATURE?</div>
        <div class="action">Beat. Everyone stares at her. JESSICA immediately starts typing.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(typing, muttering)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Fire equals feature... literally genius...</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(sitting down slowly, defeated)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh no.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(wiping forehead, quietly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh boy.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(slight smile)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Interesting.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(still confused)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Wait, what are we talking about again? The toaster?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(ignoring Ron, energized)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Let's workshop this, people! This is what we do! We don't see problems, we see possibilities!</div>
        <div class="action">Lights shift slightly as BRENDA clicks to next slide: "SELF-CLEANING OR SELF-DESTRUCT? A STRATEGIC DISCUSSION"</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(head in hands)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We're all going to jail.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calmly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly.</div>
        <div class="act-heading">ACT 2: ESCALATION</div>
        <div class="action">Continuing from Act 1. BRENDA is energized, pacing. DEREK looks defeated. Others are engaged.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pacing, gesturing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Think about it, people! We're not selling ovens that burn down houses—</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(muttering)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We literally are though.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(ignoring him, building)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We're selling ovens that create opportunities! Opportunities for home renovation! For fresh starts! For... for reimagining your living space!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing up, excited)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh my GOD, Brenda, that's literally brilliant! We could literally partner with home insurance companies!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing, incredulous)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Are you— are you serious right now?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Jessica, ignoring Derek)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Jessica, write that down! Insurance partnerships! Contractor referral programs!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(typing frantically)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">This is literally going to disrupt the entire home appliance industry!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to the room)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">It's going to disrupt people's lives! People are losing their HOMES!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(spinning to face him)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">And getting NEW homes, Derek! Better homes! Homes they actually want!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(perking up)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I like new homes. I have four of them.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quietly, to Derek)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Technically, she's not wrong about the "new homes" part...</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Todd, betrayed)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Todd!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quickly backtracking, wiping forehead)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I mean, technically, she's also not right! Technically speaking. Technically.</div>
        <div class="action">Derek's phone buzzes. He looks at it, his face falls.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(reading phone)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Another one. Phoenix, Arizona. Family of four displaced.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(immediately spinning it)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly displaced.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nodding approvingly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Très bien.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(showing phone)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">There's a photo! The house is literally a pile of ash!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(examining phone, unruffled)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Hmm. You know, in 1987, there was a case— *Toastmaster v. The People of New Jersey*—where a toaster was ruled not responsible for burning toast.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(grabbing phone back)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's completely different!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(philosophical)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Is it though? Is it really? Ze toaster gets hot. Ze toast burns. But who put ze bread in ze toaster? Ze user.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(excited)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! Exactly! User error!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(continuing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Ze oven gets hot. Ze house burns. But who put ze house around ze oven? Also ze user.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(sputtering)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's not— you can't— that's insane!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(confused but engaged)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Wait, I'm lost. Are we talking about the toaster or the microwave?</div>
        <div class="character">EVERYONE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(various responses)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">The oven!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nodding)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Right, right. The oven.</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(beat)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What's an oven?</div>
        <div class="action">Todd raises his hand tentatively.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nervous)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Um, if I could just explain the technical issue here—</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(encouraging)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! Todd! Give us the engineering perspective!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing, wiping forehead, speaking quickly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Well, technically speaking, the self-cleaning cycle activates a pyrolytic process that elevates the internal temperature to approximately 880 to 900 degrees Fahrenheit, which, technically, creates an exothermic reaction that could, theoretically, interact with combustible materials in the surrounding environment, leading to what we might call, technically speaking, a rapid oxidation event—</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(interrupting)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">A FIRE! He means a FIRE!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quickly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Technically, yes, but—</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Todd)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Todd, just say it! The oven is broken! The design is flawed!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(sweating more, conflicted)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Well, I wouldn't say "broken" exactly... more like... aggressively functional?</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(writing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Ooh, "aggressively functional!" That's literally perfect for the marketing materials!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Jessica)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Stop writing things down!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(moving to the presentation screen, clicking to new slide)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Okay, okay, let's look at the data from a different angle.</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(slide shows pie chart)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes, 40% of our ovens have caused fires. But that means 60% DIDN'T!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's not— that's not how safety works!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pointing at chart)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's a 60% success rate! That's a D-minus! That's passing!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(desperate)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">A D-minus is not passing! And we're not in school, we're selling APPLIANCES!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(helpfully)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Actually, at my college, a D-minus was literally passing.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Jessica)</div>
        <div class="action">NOT HELPING!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(clicking to next slide: customer testimonials)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">And look at this! Customer satisfaction is very high among survivors!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(freezing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I'm sorry, did you just say "survivors"?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(not seeing the problem)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! 4.5 stars on average!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(slowly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Survivors. You said survivors. As in people who survived using our product.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(excited)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">That's literally such a powerful testimonial angle! "Survivor stories!"</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(losing it)</div>
        <div class="action">THAT'S NOT A SELLING POINT!</div>
        <div class="action">Derek's phone buzzes again. And again. And again.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(looking at phone, increasingly panicked)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Seattle. Portland. Denver. These are all from today!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(undeterred, clicking to next slide)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Which brings me to my next point: rebranding!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(sitting down, head in hands)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh god.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(enthusiastic)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">The problem isn't the oven. The problem is the messaging! We're calling it "self-cleaning" which sounds so... mundane!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(engaged)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Literally so boring!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What if we called it... "Thermal Reset Technology"?</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(considering)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Hmm. Or perhaps... "Controlled Combustion Event"?</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(getting into it despite himself)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">"Extreme Clean Mode"?</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(excited)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">"PyroClean™"!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pointing at Jessica)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! I love that! PyroClean™! It sounds premium!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(head still in hands)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">It sounds like arson.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(suddenly engaged)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I like the one with the fire.</div>
        <div class="character">EVERYONE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(turning to him)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Which one?</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(confused)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">...yes?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to the group)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">See? Ron gets it! This is about perception! We don't have a product problem, we have a branding problem!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing up, slamming folder on table)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">NO! No, no, no! We have a SAFETY problem! People are losing their homes! Their possessions! Their sense of security!</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(impassioned)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We have a moral obligation to recall this product and fix it before someone gets seriously hurt!</div>
        <div class="action">Powerful silence. Everyone stares at Derek. For a moment, it seems like he's gotten through to them.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(after a long pause)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">...are we still talking about the toaster?</div>
        <div class="action">Derek slowly sits back down, defeated.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quietly, patting Derek's shoulder)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Technically... you're not wrong.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(quietly, to himself)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We're all going to jail.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calmly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(clapping hands together)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Great discussion, everyone! Really productive! Now let's talk rollout strategy—</div>
        <div class="action">Suddenly, a FIRE ALARM starts blaring. Red lights flash.</div>
        <div class="act-heading">ACT 3: RESOLUTION</div>
        <div class="action">Continuing from Act 2. FIRE ALARM is blaring. Red lights flashing. Everyone looks around confused.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(looking up)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh my god, is that literally a fire alarm?</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(checking his phone, face going pale)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Uh... guys?</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(annoyed by interruption)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What is it, Todd?</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(reading phone)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I'm getting an alert from the test kitchen... they were, uh... they were demonstrating the self-cleaning feature for the promotional video...</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(standing up slowly)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">No.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(continuing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">...and, uh, technically speaking... the kitchen is... on fire.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(vindicated but horrified)</div>
        <div class="action">I TOLD YOU! I TOLD ALL OF YOU!</div>
        <div class="action">Everyone starts grabbing their belongings in a panic. Papers flying. Coffee spilling. Chaos.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calmly gathering his briefcase)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly on fire.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pointing at the door where smoke is visible)</div>
        <div class="action">YOU CAN SEE THE SMOKE, MAURICE!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(heading toward door)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly visible smoke.</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pulling out her phone, filming)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh my god, this is literally going viral! I'm literally live-streaming this!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(still in marketing mode, even while evacuating)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Jessica, good thinking! This is actually great content! Very authentic! Very relatable!</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(grabbing his folders)</div>
        <div class="action">RELATABLE?! A FIRE IS RELATABLE?!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(heading toward door, still gesturing)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">User-generated crisis content! It's very on-brand!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(panicking, wiping forehead frantically)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Technically, we should probably evacuate! Technically speaking, immediately!</div>
        <div class="action">Everyone is moving toward the door. RON stands up slowly, calmly, as if nothing is happening. Everyone stops and turns to look at him.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calm, authoritative)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Wait.</div>
        <div class="character">EVERYONE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(stopping, turning)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What?!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pause, looking around at everyone)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I've heard everyone's input. I've reviewed the data.</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(another pause)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">And I've made my decision.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(hopeful)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">You're issuing the recall?</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(shaking his head)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">No.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(deflating)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh god.</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(decisive)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We're calling it a feature.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(exploding)</div>
        <div class="action">WHAT?!</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(pumping fist)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes! I knew it!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(filming, excited)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">This is literally the best decision ever!</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(nodding)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Très sage. Very wise.</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to Derek, apologetically)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Technically, he is the CEO...</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(backing toward door, gesturing at the smoke)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">There is LITERALLY a fire happening RIGHT NOW because of our product!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(calm, heading toward door)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(losing his mind)</div>
        <div class="action">YOU CAN'T "ALLEGEDLY" A FIRE THAT'S CURRENTLY BURNING!</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(stopping at the door, turning back)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Also, I've made another decision.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(eager)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Yes, sir?</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(matter-of-fact)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We're pivoting to refrigerators. Much safer.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(enthusiastic)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Brilliant! I love it!</div>
        <div class="character">JESSICA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(filming)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Literally so smart!</div>
        <div class="character">TODD</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(relieved)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Oh thank god.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(hopeful)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Wait, really? We're discontinuing the ovens?</div>
        <div class="character">RON</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(confused)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">What's a refrigerator?</div>
        <div class="action">Beat. Everyone stares at him.</div>
        <div class="character">BRENDA</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(ushering him out)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">We'll explain on the way out, sir!</div>
        <div class="action">Everyone rushes out. DEREK is last, stopping at the door to look back at the boardroom, shaking his head in disbelief.</div>
        <div class="character">DEREK</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to himself)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">I should've been a teacher.</div>
        <div class="action">He exits. The alarm continues blaring. Smoke gets thicker.</div>
        <div class="action">Beat.</div>
        <div class="action">MAURICE pokes his head back in, looks around.</div>
        <div class="character">MAURICE</div>
        <div class="parenthetical">(to no one)</div>
        <div class="dialogue">Allegedly.</div>
        <div class="action">He exits.</div>
        <div class="transition">BLACKOUT.</div>
        <div class="centered">TITLE CARD: "FLAMETEK INDUSTRIES STOCK ROSE 12% THE FOLLOWING DAY"</div>
        <div class="transition">FADE OUT.</div>
        <div class="action">THE END</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>